I am applying for the Software Engineer 3 - Enterprise Architecture role at M=
ongoDB.

At Black Piano, where I work as a Data Analyst, I build autonomous systems an=
d data infrastructure using Python, cloud services, and APIs. I engineered a =
self-healing data-quality agent powered by Gemini that resolves missing domai=
n records through reference-table lookups with model fallback, retries on fai=
lure, and manages escalation paths for human review. I also built custom Mode=
l Context Protocol tools to interface workflows with data pipelines, and at P=
i Software Solutions, I developed internal Python API packages to automate Bi=
gQuery access across client dashboards.

In independent projects, I architect bounded autonomous systems and multi-age=
nt harnesses. For JobAgents, I developed a Python pipeline orchestrating mult=
iple CLI harnesses over SQLite to source, deduplicate, and score thousands of=
 roles with deterministic cost gates before invoking models. In MyLocalCLI, a=
n open-source terminal assistant, I engineered parallel tool calling, dynamic=
 skill injection, and multi-provider failover. Across these implementations, =
I apply RAG, tool calling, and deterministic guardrails to keep agentic workf=
lows audit-ready, reliable, and cost-effective.

MongoDB provides the foundational document architecture for scalable, distrib=
uted systems, and I admire how its platforms enable high-throughput data acce=
ss for modern agentic applications.

I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in Python, data =
pipelines, and agent orchestration can support your Enterprise Architecture t=
eam.

